From 5e5d833208093944a8703cda2ee5bd0fa236ed8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:40:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 263/269] gallium/pvr: fix job completion waits - draws now
 complete synchronously and fences work

The completion waits were broken by a timeout convention mismatch: this kernel's syncobj wait interprets
timeout_nsec as an absolute CLOCK_MONOTONIC deadline when DRM_SYNCOBJ_WAIT_FLAGS_WAIT_FOR_SUBMIT is set
(and the reference winsys/Mesa's Vulkan runtime always uses that convention), while the driver was passing
a relative duration with no flags, so every wait failed and submits returned before the GPU was done.

All waits now go through two small helpers that pass an absolute deadline with WAIT_FOR_SUBMIT. Verified on
hardware: the compute-fallback draws complete synchronously (no "did not signal" errors, readback right
after the wait shows the final image), the two-case pipeline test still passes (512x512 default triangle:
inside=73728; 1366x768 vertex-buffer full-screen triangle: inside=1049088/1049088), the probe prints
--- ALL PASS with and without PVR_PROBE_COMPUTE_DRAW, and it prints --- ALL PASS under the drm-shim. (The
raw 3D render job still times out because the TA path itself is hardware-refused - that is the known
fixed-function blocker, not the fence plumbing.)

Also: the rasteriser shader is the guarded variant so target sizes that are not multiples of the 8x8 local
size work, and the probe exercises 1366x768 to prove it.
---
 .../pvr_native/pvr_compute_triangle_spv.h     | 376 +++++++++---------
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c    |  26 +-
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_vm.c       |  59 +--
 3 files changed, 246 insertions(+), 215 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_compute_triangle_spv.h b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_compute_triangle_spv.h
index 0872474f..0ea65d38 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_compute_triangle_spv.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_compute_triangle_spv.h
@@ -1,208 +1,224 @@
 /* Copyright 2026 The Mesa authors
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
  *
- * The compute fallback's rasteriser shader, as SPIR-V. Generated from open-perf/tri2.comp with
+ * The compute fallback's rasteriser shader, as SPIR-V. Generated from open-perf/tri4.comp with
  * glslangValidator and compiled at runtime by pco through spirv_to_nir, exactly like the reference path.
- * The parameter buffer holds three clip-space vertices followed by the target size. */
+ * The parameter buffer holds three clip-space vertices followed by the target size; the store is guarded
+ * so any target size works (pco mis-compiles an early return before a store, so the guard wraps it). */
